# Brand color palette

Use this palette for new UI (buttons, accents, embeds, illustrations). Tokens are defined in `_sass/_variables.scss` and exposed on `:root` as `--brand-*` in `_sass/_themes.scss`.

| Token | Hex | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--brand-sea` | `#3d5f5c` | Primary sea accent (hairlines, gentle fills, links) |
| `--brand-sea-deep` | `#215d42` | Deeper sea (text on light CTAs, tip blocks) |
| `--brand-rock` | `#32302d` | Dark neutral surfaces |
| `--brand-linen` | `#f8f7f5` | Page / card background |
| `--brand-ink` | `#141412` | Body text |
| `--brand-taupe` | `#8c8478` | Muted text, borders |

## Do

- Prefer `var(--brand-sea)` and siblings over one-off hex in SCSS or inline styles.
- Reuse existing patterns: `--personality-accent` maps to `--brand-sea`; earth tones in al-folio `$grey-*` / `--global-theme-color` stay for general chrome unless a feature is explicitly “sea” branded.
- For visitor CTAs, use gentle sea styling (e.g. `.contact-actions__link` in `_sass/_contact.scss`) rather than Bootstrap `btn-primary`.

## Do not

- Introduce unrelated accent colors for on-brand surfaces (no default Bootstrap blue primary for site CTAs).
- Hardcode the hex table above in multiple files — add or adjust tokens in `_variables.scss` / `_themes.scss` once.

External tools (e.g. Cal.rs) should align with linen, ink, and sea accents where configurable.
